Description: Disclosure-control tools for releasing aggregate statistics, with
    open datasets to use them on. Differential privacy: an exact discrete
    Laplace sampler for counts and the analytic Gaussian mechanism for means,
    drawing on the operating system's random source, with privacy-budget
    accounting. Checks of k-anonymity and l-diversity, and cell suppression
    audited for exact recovery from the margins. The datasets are snapshots
    of publicly available tables from open-data portals built on the
    Comprehensive Knowledge Archive Network ('CKAN', <https://ckan.org/>),
    'Socrata' (<https://dev.socrata.com/>), and 'Opendatasoft'
    (<https://www.huwise.com/>) (Chicago, New York City, Toronto, Vancouver,
    and others), Statistics Canada Canadian Centre for Justice and Community
    Safety Statistics ('CCJS') tables, a multi-agent-reviewed corpus of
    Ontario Special Investigations Unit ('SIU', <https://www.siu.on.ca/>)
    director's reports, and synthetic fixtures, with functions that read
    and verify them.
